This file contains the change history for the PPP link layer module.

People who assisted with new information on a bug are listed in brackets.

A number in square brackets refers to the Sourceforge tracker item ID.

------------------------
v1.3d6 - 28th March 2005
------------------------

- Implement LCPTerminateRequest in PPPDisconnect
- Improve debug output format for Ethereal
- Handle incoming escape sequences as per RFC [1171684] (Geoff Weiss)
- MS-CHAP v1 authentication implemented by Andrew Roughan [498031]
- Closed debug file on failed connection
- Return terrBADUSERPASS when CHAPRETRY count is reached.

-----------------------
v1.2b1 - 26th July 2003
-----------------------

- Fixed issues with output of debug information

-----------------------
v1.2d10 - 4th July 2003
-----------------------

- Modified Debug output into format compatible with Text2Pcap

----------------------------
v1.2d8 - 29th September 2002
----------------------------

- Handle LCPTerminateRequest & LCPTerminateACK
- Display LCP/IPCP code in SysFail for unsupported codes
- Resend CHAP Response after timeout without ACK/NAK
- Send CHAP tickle only if CHAP is available

---------------------------
v1.2d5 - 9th September 2002
---------------------------

- Set/Restore Data Bank register in PPPSTARTUP (CHAP Implementation error)
- Lock PPPDGMHANDLE during manipulation in PPPCONNECT

------------------------
v1.2d2 - 18th March 2002
------------------------

- CHAP with MD5 Authentication implemented by Andrew Roughan

---------------------------
v1.1f1 - 22nd February 2002
---------------------------

- Fixed problem where if serial port buffer full, and holding a packet
  of $7FFF bytes in length, and packet boundary is at the end of the
  buffer, the we could trash memory. (Andrew Roughan)
- Deleted some obsolete code in the serial port driver.
- Bumped copyright year in CDev.

---------------------------
v1.1a3 - 16th February 2002
---------------------------

- Better way of handling ping of death.

----------------------
v1.1a2 - 26th May 2001
----------------------

- New build with some memory corruption checking turned on. We'll see if
  anything pops up.

-----------------------
v1.1a1 - 11th July 1999
-----------------------

  PPP 1.1a1

- Support for link layer module interface version 2.
- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = PPP.config

=END=
